## Zig build output
##
## Added by this fork; every rule above is upstream's and is kept verbatim.
## SPDX-License-Identifier: Apache-2.0 — the grant for this fork's own files is
## recorded in FORK-LICENSE.md, not here; upstream's Apache-2.0 grant in LICENSE
## is untouched and reaches neither this section nor any other fork file.
/.zig-cache/
/zig-out/
/consumer/.zig-cache/
/consumer/zig-out/
#
# Zig 0.16 materialises a fetched dependency into a project-local directory.
# This package declares no dependencies, so these exist so that a future one -
# or a fetch a user runs by hand - cannot commit a materialised tree. The
# observed fetch for this package materialises `zig-pkg/<hash>` beside the build
# root it was run from, which is why both roots are named.
/zig-pkg/
/consumer/zig-pkg/
#
# Nix and devenv state. `direnv allow` writes `.direnv/` into this working copy,
# which sits on an NFS volume, so the entries below exist to keep a shell
# session from dirtying the tree. `.envrc` is deliberately NOT ignored: it is
# listed in build.zig.zon `.paths`, because a fetched copy whose own shell
# cannot be entered is not a whole package, and the same goes for a local
# override, which is machine state and not package content.
# `flake.lock` and `devenv.lock` are the workspace driver's to write and are
# likewise not ignored here.
/.devenv/
/.devenv.flake.nix
/devenv.local.nix
/.direnv/
/result
/result-*
